\f0\b Tuesday April 29, 2025
\f1\b0 \
Mwuahaha I\'92m back, my bad. Okay so I\'92m for sure going with the Pioneer Timesheets App.\
Today I need to think about some features I might want in this app. What features would the users (My parents / Bryan) want?\
1. [REQUIRED] User should stay logged in once account is created. (Caching)\
	1a. User is either Owner or Employee\
		ab. If user attempts to create Owner account, some form of validation will be required.\
2. [REQUIRED] Both employee and owner should have ability to create timesheet for current date or any previous date.\
	2a. Timesheet limit to 1 per day, but each timesheet can have multiple tasks.\
		ab. Tasks include driving to destination, buying material, being at shop, field work, and lunch 			(will ask dad / Bryan for any other fields).\
		ac. Hours per task\
3. [REQUIRED] Both employee and owner should be able to see past timesheets and edit them quickly.\
	3a. Only owner can see all employee timesheets [This will require CloudKit or some sort of API / web service interaction]\
	3b. Employee should only see their own timesheets.\
4. [REASONABLE] Perhaps a task board where only owner can create task for employees to then select from in their 	timesheets.\
	4a. Owner should have ability to create a task, edit and make notes for each task.\
5. [AMBITIOUS] Should also look good on iPadOS as dad would surely like to have it on his.\
\
Next up: decide which feature to start implementing first.\
